  - Reach the marker with the movement keys or left stick.
  - Shoot with the left mouse button, Space or the lower controller button.
  - Approach the marked weapon and press E or the left face button on the controller.
  - Switch slots with 1 or 2, or with the controller shoulder buttons.
  - Hold the button for the slot with the weapon you picked up to drop it.
  - Press G or the left trigger to aim, then choose where to throw. The throw starts
    the first wave.
  - Defeat the first wave and choose an upgrade card.
  - Between waves, wait or press Skip to start the next wave.
  - Watch the ranged officer. When you see its attack warning, move out of the line
    of fire. Finish the wave to see your result.
  - Reach the marker
  - Aim with the right stick to fire, or tap the attack button in single-stick mode.
  - Approach the marked weapon and tap the interaction button.
  - Tap the other weapon slot.
  - Tap the grenade button, then tap the spot to throw at. The throw starts the first
    wave.
  - Gameplay hints
  - Buy the Desert to start the first level.
  - HINT
  - A silencer reduces the noise of your shots, so fewer monsters hear you.
  - The ranged officer attacks from a distance. Move out of the marked area before
    the attack.
  - Shamans raise fallen monsters. Take the shaman out to stop the reinforcements.
  - The armored enemy takes less damage from the front. Shoot from the side or behind.
  - Champions have special traits that make them more dangerous than ordinary monsters.
  - The Hook can pull you toward it. Move aside when it winds up.
  - Use a common chest to claim its loot.
  - A locked chest needs a key. It contains a rarer weapon.
  - Opening this chest starts a fight with champions. Defeat them to claim the reward.
  - This key opens a locked chest.
  - The dome keeps monsters out and restores health. During a wave, time inside is
    limited.
  - Shoot a barrel to trigger its effect. Keep your distance when it goes off.
  - Get into a vehicle to ram monsters. The vehicle can break if it takes too much
    damage.
  - Boss attacks are telegraphed. Watch the marked zones and move before the attack
    lands.
  - The arena is locked until you defeat the boss. Winning a run with a closed arena
    grants a bonus.
  - Step onto stairs to change floors. Monsters can follow you.
  - Gargoyle
  - Leave the shadow before the Gargoyle dives. Its stone skin absorbs most damage
    for a few seconds.
